foundation.question_text:
The bar model shows the ratio $1:3$.
Complete the equivalent ratio $1:3=5:\square$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[fill=blue!25] (0,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (1,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (2,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (3,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The bar model shows the ratio $2:3$.
Write two ratios that are equivalent to $2:3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[fill=blue!25] (0,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=blue!25] (1,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (2,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (3,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\draw[fill=white] (4,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.5]
\draw[fill=blue!25] (0,0) rectangle ++(1,1);
